WEBVTT

00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:07.670
<i>This looks like Eichi's room.</i>

00:00:14.770 --> 00:00:17.070
<i>What is this cold feeling?</i>

00:00:18.800 --> 00:00:21.830
<i>A shadow filled with the smell of death</i>
<i>surrounds this house.</i>

00:00:22.370 --> 00:00:25.200
<i>Why? What's going on?!</i>

00:02:11.600 --> 00:02:15.400
You need to put it out of your mind.
That was an unfortunate accident.

00:02:16.730 --> 00:02:17.400
But...

00:02:18.100 --> 00:02:19.130
They were...

00:02:19.770 --> 00:02:22.200
They were so happy.

00:02:24.000 --> 00:02:25.700
Why did they have to...

00:02:30.170 --> 00:02:31.230
<i>No way!</i>

00:02:50.030 --> 00:02:52.570
DEAR GRANDMA,

00:02:53.330 --> 00:02:56.570
Who are you writing the postcard to?
A friend from school?

00:02:56.730 --> 00:02:58.730
No, to my grandmother.

00:03:00.230 --> 00:03:02.830
Because I left Grandma's home
in that manner.

00:03:03.400 --> 00:03:06.470
And also...because I'm
worried about her.

00:03:09.030 --> 00:03:10.430
You're very kind, Mitsuki.

00:03:10.570 --> 00:03:11.230
Huh?

00:03:11.430 --> 00:03:13.300
Because you're very considerate
of your Grandma at a time

00:03:13.330 --> 00:03:16.230
when your head is probably
filled with thoughts of Eichi.

00:03:17.000 --> 00:03:18.870
N-No it isn't.

00:03:19.170 --> 00:03:20.770
You don't have to hide it!

00:03:21.000 --> 00:03:22.230
<i>- That's right.</i>
- I'm not hiding anything!

00:03:22.270 --> 00:03:23.700
<i>- I wonder whether he figured out</i>
- But you're blushing!

00:03:23.730 --> 00:03:25.100
<i>the meaning of Eichi's name</i>
<i>appearing backwards.</i>

00:03:25.130 --> 00:03:27.670
<i>- Hey, hurry up, Takuto!</i>
- Stop it, Ms. Oshige!

00:03:31.170 --> 00:03:34.100
I can't believe it.
No way.

00:03:38.430 --> 00:03:41.070
Before it happened,
I had a bad premonition.

00:03:41.930 --> 00:03:44.570
When I think to myself
that didn't I stop them...

00:03:44.900 --> 00:03:48.130
You can't think about
stuff like that now.

00:03:49.930 --> 00:03:53.300
But they were
living so happily.

00:03:53.900 --> 00:03:56.300
To think that all three of them
had to die.

00:03:58.330 --> 00:04:00.230
That too is our fate.

00:04:00.870 --> 00:04:02.630
We have no choice
but to accept it.

00:04:06.030 --> 00:04:07.030
I can't believe it.

00:04:10.000 --> 00:04:12.370
Mitsuki worked hard
to see Eichi.

00:04:19.430 --> 00:04:21.930
<i>You want to become</i>
<i>a singer that much?</i>

00:04:22.300 --> 00:04:24.330
<i>Yep...it's a promise.</i>

00:04:24.770 --> 00:04:27.400
<i>A promise to Eichi.</i>

00:04:28.730 --> 00:04:30.630
<i>I like you, Eichi.</i>

00:04:31.570 --> 00:04:35.170
<i>I will work hard so that my songs</i>
<i>will reach you in America,</i>

00:04:35.200 --> 00:04:36.630
<i>so wait for that day.</i>

00:04:38.570 --> 00:04:43.300
<i>There's no point unless these feelings</i>
<i>are conveyed to you, Eichi.</i>

00:04:45.100 --> 00:04:46.100
<i>Eichi...</i>

00:04:48.100 --> 00:04:49.100
<i>Eichi...</i>

00:04:51.100 --> 00:04:52.170
<i>Eichi...</i>

00:04:57.470 --> 00:05:03.470
<i>Eichi... Eichi has passed away.</i>
<i>If Mitsuki finds out...</i>

00:05:07.670 --> 00:05:10.030
Those backward letters...
Don't tell me that...

00:05:24.270 --> 00:05:25.270
We'll be there soon.

00:05:26.430 --> 00:05:30.300
You'll get to see Eichi soon.
How do you feel?

00:05:30.700 --> 00:05:33.430
You probably feel like you've
grown wings and can fly, right?

00:05:34.000 --> 00:05:38.230
Yes, because I've worked hard till now
just so I could see Eichi again.

00:05:38.900 --> 00:05:42.600
I see. If we continue down this road,
we'll get there.

00:05:42.900 --> 00:05:44.330
Just be patient a little longer.

00:05:44.600 --> 00:05:45.600
Okay.

00:05:45.900 --> 00:05:49.230
<i>Takuto... What should we do?</i>
<i>We're almost there.</i>

00:06:00.500 --> 00:06:01.970
What happened?

00:06:02.200 --> 00:06:03.830
Could it be a flat tire?

00:06:04.030 --> 00:06:06.700
I don't know,
but the car suddenly veered.

00:06:07.270 --> 00:06:08.970
In any case,
let me take a look.

00:06:09.130 --> 00:06:10.130
I'll look too.

00:06:14.800 --> 00:06:17.070
Man, just when we
were almost there.

00:06:25.230 --> 00:06:27.130
- Takuto...
- Huh? Takuto?

00:06:30.500 --> 00:06:32.630
Could this be Takuto's doing?

00:06:33.300 --> 00:06:34.300
What is it?

00:06:34.600 --> 00:06:35.270
It's a flat tire.

00:06:36.400 --> 00:06:38.670
Takuto!
Where in the world were you?

00:06:39.170 --> 00:06:40.170
Go home right now!

00:06:40.200 --> 00:06:40.870
Huh?

00:06:43.070 --> 00:06:44.430
What?! Why?!

00:06:44.630 --> 00:06:46.770
Because! Just go home!

00:06:46.900 --> 00:06:49.170
No way! Tell me the reason!

00:06:49.200 --> 00:06:51.200
I don't have a reason!
Just go home!

00:06:51.330 --> 00:06:55.030
<i>It looks like it would be better</i>
<i>not to go to Eichi's house after all.</i>

00:06:56.400 --> 00:06:58.670
Shall we go home for today?

00:06:58.700 --> 00:07:00.170
Huh?! Why?!

00:07:01.300 --> 00:07:03.400
You see, it was written in
the Death Spirit Handbook

00:07:03.430 --> 00:07:05.630
that today is
a day of bad fortune!

00:07:05.670 --> 00:07:06.330
Huh?

00:07:06.370 --> 00:07:09.270
Stop! Stop! Stop!
Let's call this off for today!

00:07:09.400 --> 00:07:11.070
If today's no good,
then when is?

00:07:11.100 --> 00:07:14.270
Umm... Next week...
Let's do it next week!

00:07:15.700 --> 00:07:16.370
See...

00:07:16.400 --> 00:07:19.430
It's good fortune to visit
people next week. See?

00:07:19.470 --> 00:07:20.470
Huh?

00:07:20.700 --> 00:07:22.700
It doesn't matter!
We're going to turn back!

00:07:22.930 --> 00:07:26.330
Why?! I'm so close to seeing Eichi!

00:07:28.130 --> 00:07:29.770
I can't let you see Eichi.

00:07:30.630 --> 00:07:31.630
Why?!

00:07:31.830 --> 00:07:32.830
You just can't.

00:07:33.000 --> 00:07:36.330
You're awful!
Why do you say such mean things?!

00:07:36.470 --> 00:07:37.830
That's right, I'm mean!

00:07:38.130 --> 00:07:39.830
That's exactly what I am.
A mean guy!

00:07:44.070 --> 00:07:45.800
Where's Mitsuki?

00:07:46.270 --> 00:07:51.430
She's probably talking to Takuto.
But the mood feels different than usual.

00:07:52.370 --> 00:07:55.270
Look, when I say you can't go,
I mean you can't go.

00:07:56.030 --> 00:07:57.030
- Please understand.
- No.

00:07:58.070 --> 00:08:01.670
Even if you say I can't,
Takuto, I will go...by myself.

00:08:02.370 --> 00:08:03.370
H-Hey!

00:08:04.870 --> 00:08:08.070
That's absurd,
saying you'll go alone!

00:08:08.830 --> 00:08:10.630
Come on,
let's go home, Mitsuki.

00:08:13.070 --> 00:08:14.370
Hey, Mitsuki!

00:08:19.570 --> 00:08:21.300
<i>Could that be...</i>

00:08:22.230 --> 00:08:23.530
<i>Eichi's house?!</i>

00:08:24.400 --> 00:08:28.230
Hey, Mitsuki! Don't go!
Today just isn't good!

00:08:30.100 --> 00:08:30.770
No!

00:08:30.930 --> 00:08:33.230
I will not let you go!

00:08:36.230 --> 00:08:36.900
Mitsuki!

00:08:37.200 --> 00:08:39.070
I have been living for this day.

00:08:40.730 --> 00:08:45.530
If I can't see Eichi, then what is
the meaning of all my perseverance?

00:08:46.170 --> 00:08:49.230
I know that.
I know all that.

00:08:49.570 --> 00:08:51.900
Then why are you
getting in my way?

00:08:52.230 --> 00:08:54.400
Eichi is so near!

00:08:55.000 --> 00:08:57.300
You're wrong.
It's not like that.

00:08:58.870 --> 00:09:00.630
Eichi isn't there.

00:09:00.830 --> 00:09:01.500
Huh?

00:09:02.800 --> 00:09:03.800
He isn't there.

00:09:04.330 --> 00:09:06.300
I don't understand
what you're saying!

00:09:07.370 --> 00:09:10.430
I can't tell you more than this.
In any case, Eichi isn't there.

00:09:10.830 --> 00:09:12.030
So let's go home.

00:09:12.670 --> 00:09:14.000
Why isn't he there?

00:09:15.200 --> 00:09:16.200
Why?!

00:09:26.930 --> 00:09:28.870
Takuto!
Shouldn't you stop her?

00:09:29.470 --> 00:09:30.700
- I can't stop her.
- Huh?

00:09:32.030 --> 00:09:34.270
I saw that expression
on her face.

00:09:35.070 --> 00:09:36.070
I can't.

00:09:38.670 --> 00:09:43.370
That Takuto... He always says
weird things when it comes to Eichi.

00:09:46.400 --> 00:09:49.970
But I wonder what he meant
when he said Eichi isn't there?

00:10:42.930 --> 00:10:46.630
Umm... Is this Eichi Sakurai's house?

00:10:47.970 --> 00:10:49.600
Yes. Who are you?

00:10:50.300 --> 00:10:52.600
My name is Mitsuki Koyama.

00:10:53.000 --> 00:10:55.430
I came from Japan because
I wanted to see Eichi.

00:10:55.930 --> 00:10:59.330
M-My goodness.
That's very far.

00:11:00.030 --> 00:11:02.700
Please come in.

00:11:03.700 --> 00:11:04.700
Thank you.

00:11:08.470 --> 00:11:09.930
I apologize for coming here
out of the blue like this.

00:11:10.170 --> 00:11:12.670
But I wanted to
surprise Eichi.

00:11:13.700 --> 00:11:14.730
Who is this girl?

00:11:15.400 --> 00:11:17.200
She came from Japan
to see Eichi.

00:11:17.470 --> 00:11:18.130
What?

00:11:18.370 --> 00:11:19.370
How do you do?

00:11:20.100 --> 00:11:22.070
Umm... Where is Eichi?

00:11:26.230 --> 00:11:27.570
A photo of Eichi!

00:11:31.270 --> 00:11:33.130
Eichi isn't here.

00:11:34.400 --> 00:11:36.970
U-Umm... What do you mean?

00:11:38.270 --> 00:11:42.330
Eichi died two years ago.

00:11:58.000 --> 00:12:01.570
Eichi died two years ago.

00:12:02.230 --> 00:12:02.900
Huh?

00:12:03.570 --> 00:12:07.630
My son and daughter-in-law
adopted Eichi,

00:12:07.670 --> 00:12:10.100
but all three of them died
in an automobile accident.

00:12:12.630 --> 00:12:15.030
He...died?

00:12:22.830 --> 00:12:23.970
<i>Mitsuki!</i>

00:12:26.530 --> 00:12:30.700
Eichi...died?

00:12:35.230 --> 00:12:37.570
That can't be true.
No way.

00:12:38.130 --> 00:12:41.800
That means that...
that Mitsuki's wish...

00:12:43.770 --> 00:12:44.800
Mitsuki.

00:12:46.970 --> 00:12:47.970
Here.

00:12:48.830 --> 00:12:54.230
TO MITSUKI
This is a letter that Eichi left behind.
I've kept it unopened.

00:12:56.700 --> 00:13:00.000
He probably never
intended to send it.

00:13:01.130 --> 00:13:04.330
TO MITSUKI
I'm sorry that I have to give it to you
under these circumstances.

00:13:07.470 --> 00:13:10.430
TO MITSUKI

00:13:17.000 --> 00:13:18.000
Mitsuki!

00:13:18.470 --> 00:13:19.470
Mitsuki!

00:13:20.870 --> 00:13:22.500
Mitsuki! Mitsuki!

00:13:40.600 --> 00:13:42.030
She finally fell asleep.

00:13:46.170 --> 00:13:47.170
I see.

00:13:48.170 --> 00:13:49.930
All that had happened...

00:13:50.700 --> 00:13:54.270
I'm so sorry that you came
all the way from Japan.

00:13:54.730 --> 00:13:56.200
Don't worry about us.

00:13:58.070 --> 00:13:59.230
But Mitsuki...

00:14:00.230 --> 00:14:02.870
When I think of how
Mitsuki must be feeling...

00:14:07.930 --> 00:14:10.800
Please stay awhile.

00:14:11.370 --> 00:14:12.430
Thank you very much.

00:14:13.900 --> 00:14:16.530
Why kind of a boy was Eichi?

00:14:17.670 --> 00:14:22.070
He was a quiet
but thoughtful boy.

00:14:23.130 --> 00:14:25.830
He gradually became
accustomed to living here

00:14:25.870 --> 00:14:28.730
and had just started
making a few friends.

00:14:30.600 --> 00:14:31.600
But...

00:14:49.000 --> 00:14:51.030
Mitsuki... I'm coming in.

00:15:07.170 --> 00:15:08.230
<i>Eichi...</i>

00:15:11.930 --> 00:15:12.930
Mitsuki!

00:15:13.300 --> 00:15:14.370
Mitsuki!

00:15:14.730 --> 00:15:16.030
Mitsuki!

00:15:16.870 --> 00:15:19.900
Mitsuki! Where are you?

00:15:28.700 --> 00:15:31.770
<i>Eichi... Where are you?</i>

00:15:33.100 --> 00:15:35.570
<i>Eichi... Answer me.</i>

00:15:37.130 --> 00:15:38.970
<i>Eichi isn't there.</i>

00:15:41.030 --> 00:15:45.600
Why do you...
Why do you say things like that?

00:15:46.600 --> 00:15:47.600
Eichi...

00:15:54.670 --> 00:15:55.870
What's this?

00:15:58.970 --> 00:16:00.970
Eichi's...handwriting.

00:16:08.300 --> 00:16:11.470
<i>Two months have passed since</i>
<i>I began living here in America</i>

00:16:11.500 --> 00:16:16.370
<i>and I've come to realize</i>
<i>that I really do like you.</i>

00:16:18.770 --> 00:16:21.370
<i>I like you even more than</i>
<i>I did when we lived together.</i>

00:16:22.570 --> 00:16:25.870
<i>But I wonder if</i>
<i>you will forget me.</i>

00:16:27.900 --> 00:16:33.230
<i>When I think that you may forget me</i>
<i>as time passes and we grow up...</i>

00:16:33.830 --> 00:16:35.300
<i>To be honest, it's unsettling.</i>

00:16:37.870 --> 00:16:41.770
<i>I don't want you to know that</i>
<i>I am such a pathetic man.</i>

00:16:42.670 --> 00:16:46.430
<i>But it's okay since this is a letter</i>
<i>that you will never read.</i>

00:16:47.770 --> 00:16:50.430
<i>I will express</i>
<i>my feelings honestly.</i>

00:16:54.330 --> 00:16:56.330
<i>Mitsuki, I like you so much.</i>

00:16:58.770 --> 00:17:00.600
<i>I like your sparkling eyes.</i>

00:17:01.700 --> 00:17:03.330
<i>The way you live life</i>
<i>to the fullest.</i>

00:17:05.300 --> 00:17:06.570
<i>Your dedication.</i>

00:17:08.630 --> 00:17:10.330
<i>The tranquility of your voice</i>
<i>when you sing.</i>

00:17:11.030 --> 00:17:13.130
<i>I wanted to tell you</i>
<i>I've always liked you.</i>

00:17:15.900 --> 00:17:17.970
<i>I wish I had told you</i>
<i>many times that I liked you.</i>

00:17:19.170 --> 00:17:21.570
<i>But I was too shy to say it.</i>

00:17:24.970 --> 00:17:27.100
<i>But someday</i>
<i>we will meet again.</i>

00:17:28.100 --> 00:17:33.230
<i>And that's when I'll tell you</i>
<i>that I like you...</i>

00:17:33.270 --> 00:17:34.900
<i>until my voice is hoarse.</i>

00:17:42.700 --> 00:17:46.230
Eichi... Where are you?

00:17:49.830 --> 00:17:50.930
I want to see you.

00:19:09.570 --> 00:19:10.900
Eichi...

00:19:16.030 --> 00:19:17.800
This is where you were?

00:19:21.470 --> 00:19:22.470
Eichi...

00:19:24.300 --> 00:19:25.870
<i>Wait!</i>

00:19:29.000 --> 00:19:31.470
<i>Wait, Eichi!</i>

00:19:37.700 --> 00:19:39.870
<i>Wait, Eichi!</i>

00:19:40.800 --> 00:19:42.070
<i>Eichi!</i>

00:19:44.170 --> 00:19:45.430
<i>Eichi!</i>

00:19:51.230 --> 00:19:52.230
<i>I caught you!</i>

00:20:18.430 --> 00:20:19.670
<i>I can stop now, right?</i>

00:20:20.400 --> 00:20:23.270
<i>I worked so hard</i>
<i>up to this point.</i>

00:20:24.900 --> 00:20:28.570
<i>I persevered believing</i>
<i>that I would see you, Eichi.</i>

00:20:34.630 --> 00:20:39.130
<i>But...I don't have to</i>
<i>persevere anymore, do I?</i>

00:20:40.730 --> 00:20:43.770
Mitsuki, where are you?!

00:20:44.030 --> 00:20:45.430
Answer us!

00:20:45.730 --> 00:20:47.330
Mitsuki!

00:20:48.970 --> 00:20:49.630
<i>Mitsuki...</i>

00:20:49.800 --> 00:20:54.370
<i>Can't I be some kind</i>
<i>of support for you?!</i>

00:21:00.130 --> 00:21:02.930
<i>I'll go to sleep here just like this.</i>

00:21:03.500 --> 00:21:08.770
<i>If I do that, I'll probably be by</i>
<i>Eichi's side when I wake up.</i>

00:21:09.530 --> 00:21:13.270
<i>I won't let anyone get between</i>
<i>me and Eichi any longer.</i>

00:21:14.570 --> 00:21:23.700
<i>Eichi, please hurry and get me.</i>
<i>I'm here. I'll be right here.</i>

00:21:26.670 --> 00:21:30.130
<i>Come here by my side, Eichi.</i>

00:21:32.430 --> 00:21:33.770
<i>Hurry to me.</i>

00:23:06.870 --> 00:23:08.900
I can't believe it.
Eichi is...

00:23:10.730 --> 00:23:14.330
What are we supposed to
say to her at a time like this?!

00:23:15.070 --> 00:23:16.070
Takuto...

00:23:16.630 --> 00:23:22.330
I won't give up.
I'll...I'll make her want to sing again!

00:23:23.570 --> 00:23:25.500
I won't let it all come
to an end like this!

00:23:26.800 --> 00:23:31.300
Next time on Full Moon:
"I Won't Sing Ever Again!"

00:23:32.030 --> 00:23:33.030
- Look forward to it!
- Look forward to it!
